## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's ability to translate product goals into a financially grounded technical plan, balancing on-device ML costs, user privacy, and rollout risk.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML cost modeling (energy, memory, inference latency)
- Data transfer savings and network impact
- Privacy controls and regulatory compliance
- OTA update cadence and maintenance costs
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost model for CBA calculations
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.inferences * params.energyPerInference;
  const memory = params.modelSize + params.cacheSize;
  const dataSavings = params.uploadSize * params.reductionRate;
  return { energy, memory, dataSavings };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to model costs for on-device features with privacy constraints, focusing on storage, compute, telemetry, and go/no-go criteria. It emphasizes practical trade-offs and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- On-device compute budgeting
- Data minimization and privacy compliance
- Telemetry design and cost optimization
- Index sizing and update cadence
- Break-even analysis and milestone-driven go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params) {
  const storageCost = params.indexMB * 0.15;
  const energyCost = params.annualWh * 0.0003;
  const telemetryCost = params.dailyTelemetryKB * 365 * 0.00001;
  const privacyAuditCost = params.userCount * 0.10;

  return {
    storageCost,
    energyCost,
    telemetryCost,
    privacyAuditCost,
    totalYear1Cost: storageCost + energyCost + telemetryCost + privacyAuditCost
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes the ability to quantify costs and plan a privacy-preserving edge learning deployment with strict safety constraints, OTA updates, and phased rollout across a fleet.

## Key Concepts
- On-device RL combined with federated updates
- Resource budgeting: energy, memory, CPU, bandwidth
- Privacy/compliance costs and safety validation
- Rollout strategy, offline fallback, drift monitoring, maintenance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Budget calculation (pseudo)
function estimateBudget(params) {
  const energy = params.rlEnergy * params.updateFreq;
  const mem = params.bufferSize * 1.5;
  return { energy, mem };
}
```

