## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design a financially justified, privacy-conscious payment feature that hinges on hardware-assisted security. It requires mapping costs to real-world constraints (region rollout, compliance, energy), and deriving Go/No-Go thresholds with a clear break-even horizon.

## Key Concepts

- On-device security (TEE, secure element)
- Card-not-present risk scoring and decision latency
- Multi-region rollout and regulatory compliance
- Cost drivers: licensing, key management, telemetry, energy
- Break-even calculation and ROI signaling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo on-device risk decision (sketch)
function shouldAuthorizeLocally(riskScore, latencyMs) {
  const threshold = 0.6;
  const fastPath = latencyMs < 200;
  return riskScore < threshold && fastPath;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate regional data privacy compliance and audits?
- What telemetry would you collect to monitor drift without leaking PII?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design cost-aware, privacy-preserving on-device learning with federation. Evaluate cross-app data leverage, regulatory implications, and rollout strategy across regions.

## Key Concepts

- Federated learning and secure aggregation
- On-device resource budgeting (CPU, memory, energy)
- Model drift telemetry and anomaly tracking
- Regulatory/compliance costs and rollout governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: federated update cycle outline
while (serviceRunning) {
  const localBatch = collectLocalSignals();
  const grads = computeGradients(localBatch);
  const encGrads = secureAggregate(grads);
  sendToServer(encGrads);
  updateLocalModelIfNeeded();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure drift and trigger model refresh?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate ROI without exposing data?
